module lysisDetection
module aktKinaseDetection
module gapdhActivityDetection

manifest HepG2_Cells
manifest EaglesMEM_10FBS_PenStrep
manifest SerumFreeMedium
manifest Insulin
manifest CellTrackerOrange
manifest PBS
manifest LysisBuffer
manifest BSA_PBS
manifest AktAssayBuffer
manifest GapdhAssayBuffer
manifest DeionizedWater

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Microfluidic Probe for Single-Cell Analysis in Adherent
// Tissue Culture
// Sarkar, Kolitz, Lauffenburger, Han --
// Nature Communications 5:3421, 2014.
// DOI: 10.1038/ncomms4421
//
// Protocol: Selective hydrodynamic confinement-based lysis
// of single adherent HepG2 cells from standard tissue
// culture, followed by lysate capture, mixing with assay
// buffers, pneumatic valve-based chamber trapping, and
// multiplexed fluorescence activity measurement of kinase
// Akt (Sox peptide sensor) and housekeeping enzyme GAPDH
// (NADH formation) simultaneously from the same cell.
//
// Device: Three-layer PDMS microfluidic probe.
//   Layer 1 (base): bare glass slide (except at tip)
//   Layer 2 (membrane): ~30 um thin PDMS; forms deformable
//     tip base; contains pneumatic valve lines (V1-V4)
//   Layer 3 (flow): ~5 mm thick PDMS; contains channels,
//     reaction chambers (AB1-AB4), and flow/control ports.
//   Tip channels: 5 um tall (lysis + assay buffer mixing)
//   Reaction chambers: 30 um tall (maximise fluorescence)
//   Assay volume per chamber: ~20 nL
//
// LYSIS ZONE PRINCIPLE: Simultaneous Qout (central channel,
//   lysis buffer outflow, 5 nL/min) and Qin (outer channels,
//   inflow, 50 nL/min total; 25 nL/min per outer channel)
//   create a hydrodynamically confined lysis zone of radius
//   R tunable by Qin/Qout ratio. Zone set slightly smaller
//   than cell diameter (~15 um) to lyse only target cell.
//   Lysis buffer detergent (1% Triton X-100) confined to zone;
//   neighbouring cells remain unaffected even at ~80%
//   confluency. Lysate captured within ~20 s after lysis.
//
// MIXING RATIO: Lysate:assay buffer = 1:4 (set by flow
//   resistance ratio of lysate and assay buffer channels).
//   Repeatability of mixing ratio within 10% CV.
//   Travel time from tip to reaction chamber: 90 s.
//
// MULTIPLEXED ARM (this .bs file): Lysate from a single
//   HepG2 cell subdivided into two chambers -- AB1 (Akt
//   Sox sensor assay) and AB2 (GAPDH NADH assay) -- via
//   pneumatic valve routing. Primary result: Fig. 5 (n=12).
//   Single-activity arms (Akt only: Fig. 4a; GAPDH only:
//   Fig. 4b) are not separately encoded here; they differ
//   only in lysate routing (one chamber instead of two).
//
// NOTE ON `mix` ABSTRACTION:
//   (a) Device priming / BSA coating: `mix` abstracts
//       syringe-pump-driven flow through device channels.
//   (b) Cell labelling and stimulation: `mix` abstracts
//       incubation of cells with dye or insulin in medium.
//   (c) Lysis zone formation: `mix` abstracts simultaneous
//       Qout/Qin flow at probe tip creating lysis zone.
//   (d) Lysate + assay buffer mixing: `mix` abstracts
//       passive resistance-ratio mixing in flow channels
//       before entering reaction chambers.
//   None of these are DMF electrode mixing steps.
//
// NOTE ON TEMPERATURE:
//   Cell culture, labelling, and recovery: 37 C / 5% CO2.
//   Assay chamber monitoring: 30 C (heating chamber,
//     Tokai Hit; lower than 37 C to reduce photobleaching).
//   BioScript `heat` models both incubator and heating stage.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS:
//   BioScript supports s and m only; h not supported.
//   Serum starvation 12-24 h -> 720m (minimum, 12 h)
//   Cell attachment 4-16 h -> 240m (minimum, 4 h)
//   BSA coating: 60m (1 h at 50 nL/min)
//   UV bleach: 30m
//   Cell Tracker labelling: 15m-45m -> 15m (minimum)
//   Cell recovery post-labelling: 20m-45m -> 20m (minimum)
//   Stimulation (insulin for Akt): 10m-16.5m -> 10m
//   Lysis + capture: ~20 s -> 20s
//   Valve travel time: 90 s
//   Assay imaging: 20m minimum
//   Clonal expansion: not in this protocol
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: device priming, BSA
//                            coating, UV bleach, cell
//                            culture, serum starvation,
//                            cell labelling, insulin
//                            stimulation, lysis zone,
//                            lysate capture
//   BB2  lysisPass         -- lysisSignal > 0: lysis
//                            confirmed (Cell Tracker Orange
//                            fluorescence drop in target
//                            cell); proceed to assay
//   BB3  lysisFail         -- lysisSignal <= 0: lysis
//                            failed (no fluorescence drop
//                            or neighbouring cell affected);
//                            drain lysis zone and retry
//   BB4  lysisJoin         -- join: Akt assay branch begins
//   BB5  aktPass           -- aktSignal > 0: Akt activity
//                            detected above lysis buffer
//                            control baseline; dispose
//   BB6  aktFail           -- aktSignal <= 0: no Akt signal
//                            (possible 'low Akt' phenotype
//                            or cell non-responsive to
//                            insulin); drain Akt chamber
//   BB7  aktJoin           -- join: GAPDH assay branch begins
//   BB8  gapdhPass         -- gapdhSignal > 0: GAPDH
//                            activity detected (housekeeping
//                            loading control confirmed);
//                            dispose assay mixture
//   BB9  gapdhFail         -- gapdhSignal <= 0: GAPDH
//                            not detected; drain chamber
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose GAPDH
//                            signal; NOP
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Device preparation -- DI water priming.
//         Prime channels with de-ionised water using gas-tight
//         glass syringes (50 uL) connected to lysis buffer
//         and inflow source ports via fused silica tubing
//         (OD 360 um, ID 100 um). Controlled by syringe pumps
//         (Harvard Apparatus PHD 2000).
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts syringe-pump flow through
//         device channels at low flow rate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

diWater       = dispense 1 units of DeionizedWater
primedDevice  = mix diWater with diWater for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Device preparation -- BSA coating.
//         Coat device channels with 1% BSA in 0.5x PBS to
//         prevent non-specific protein binding to PDMS surfaces.
//         Drawn in at 50 nL/min for at least 1 h (60 min),
//         then washed with de-ionised water.
//         BSA coating is critical to preserve enzyme activity
//         from the picomolar single-cell lysate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaPbs        = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
diWash        = dispense 1 units of DeionizedWater
bsaCoated     = mix primedDevice with bsaPbs for 60m

heat bsaCoated at 25c for 60m

bsaWashed     = mix bsaCoated with diWash for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Device preparation -- UV photobleaching.
//         Bleach the area of device observed during assay for
//         at least 30 min using UV light (ex 377 nm) to reduce
//         background fluorescence in reaction chambers.
//         Done immediately before loading assay buffers and
//         before placing the plate on the microscope stage.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat bsaWashed at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Load assay buffers into reservoirs.
//         Immediately before use, lysis buffer loaded into
//         syringe at lysis buffer port.
//         Akt assay buffer (50 mM Tris-HCl pH 7.3, 10 mM
//         MgCl2, 1 mM EGTA, 2 mM DTT, 4 mM PKC inhibitor
//         peptide, 10 mM Sox substrate peptide, 1 mM ATP,
//         0.4 mM PKItide, 5 uM GF109203X) loaded into AB1.
//         GAPDH assay buffer (90 mM sodium pyrophosphate pH
//         7.1, 20 mM NaH2PO4, 3 mM DTT, 4 mM NAD+, 10 mM
//         glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate) loaded into AB2.
//         Each reservoir: 20 uL.
//         Lysis buffer: 50 mM beta-glycerophosphate, 10 mM
//         sodium pyrophosphate, 30 mM NaF, 50 mM Tris pH 7.4,
//         1% Triton X-100, 15 mM NaCl, 2 mM EGTA, 100 uM
//         sodium orthovanadate, 1 mM DTT, 1X protease and
//         phosphatase inhibitor cocktails, 20 ug/mL Alexa 488-
//         labelled BSA (for lysis zone visualisation).
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts passive buffer loading into
//         reservoirs; no active mixing occurs at this step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisBuffer   = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
aktBuffer     = dispense 1 units of AktAssayBuffer
gapdhBuffer   = dispense 1 units of GapdhAssayBuffer
loadedDevice  = mix bsaWashed with lysisBuffer for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Cell culture -- HepG2 plating and attachment.
//         HepG2 cells (ATCC HB-8065) plated at 5,000-20,000
//         cells/cm2 on standard tissue culture polystyrene.
//         Medium: Eagle's MEM + 10% FBS + 1% pen/strep
//         (Invitrogen). Culture at 37 C, 5% CO2.
//         Allow to attach for 4-16 h (minimum: 4 h = 240m).
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts cell seeding and medium
//         addition to tissue culture plate. `heat` models
//         37 C CO2 incubator dwell for attachment.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hepg2Cells    = dispense 1 units of HepG2_Cells
cultureMedium = dispense 1 units of EaglesMEM_10FBS_PenStrep
platedCells   = mix hepg2Cells with cultureMedium for 2m

heat platedCells at 37c for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Serum starvation (12-24 h minimum; 720m).
//         Replace complete medium with serum-free Eagle's MEM
//         to synchronise signalling state before stimulation.
//         Serum starvation sensitises Akt pathway to insulin.
//         Duration: 720m (minimum; 12 h).
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts medium exchange on plate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

serumFree     = dispense 1 units of SerumFreeMedium
starvedCells  = mix platedCells with serumFree for 2m

heat starvedCells at 37c for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Cell labelling with Cell Tracker Orange dye.
//         Incubate serum-starved cells with 2.5 uM Cell
//         Tracker Orange in serum-free medium for 15-45 min
//         at 37 C (minimum: 15m). Dye labels cytosol;
//         fluorescence drop in target cell confirms lysis.
//         Wash with PBS, then recover in serum-free medium
//         at 37 C for 20-45 min (minimum: 20m) before
//         stimulation. Imaging: rhodamine filter
//         (ex 540 nm, em 570 nm, Semrock).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellTracker   = dispense 1 units of CellTrackerOrange
labelledCells = mix starvedCells with cellTracker for 15m

heat labelledCells at 37c for 15m

pbsWash       = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedCells   = mix labelledCells with pbsWash for 2m

recoveryMedium  = dispense 1 units of SerumFreeMedium
recoveredCells  = mix washedCells with recoveryMedium for 2m

heat recoveredCells at 37c for 20m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Insulin stimulation to activate Akt.
//         Spike insulin to final concentration 500 ng/mL in
//         serum-free medium (for Akt time-course: cells lysed
//         one by one under continuous stimulation conditions;
//         medium NOT removed; cells lysed directly off plate).
//         Stimulation duration: 10-16.5 min tested;
//         here 10m (minimum tested; Fig. 4a/c/5a).
//         For serum-starved control: medium not replaced;
//         no insulin added.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts insulin addition to plate
//         medium. `heat` models 37 C incubator dwell.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

insulinStock    = dispense 1 units of Insulin
stimulatedCells = mix recoveredCells with insulinStock for 2m

heat stimulatedCells at 37c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Single-cell lysis by hydrodynamic confinement.
//         Plate transferred to microscope (Olympus IX71).
//         Microfluidic probe positioned near target HepG2 cell
//         using micromanipulator.
//         Lysis zone created by:
//           Qout (central channel): 5 nL/min lysis buffer
//           Qin (outer channels):   50 nL/min total inflow
//                                   (25 nL/min per channel)
//         Zone radius R set slightly smaller than cell (~15 um)
//         by Qin/Qout = 10 ratio (Fig. 2b of paper).
//         Target cell lysed immediately on exposure; cytosolic
//         Cell Tracker Orange fluorescence drops within ~20 s.
//         Neighbouring cell fluorescence unaffected.
//         Lysate captured by Qin inflow along outer channels.
//         Lysis confirmed by Cell Tracker Orange fluorescence
//         drop monitored on rhodamine filter (ex 540, em 570).
//         `lysisDetection` module abstracts this fluorescence
//         drop QC check on target vs. neighbouring cells.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the simultaneous Qout/Qin
//         flow at tip creating and maintaining the lysis zone.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisZone     = mix loadedDevice with stimulatedCells for 20s
lysisSignal   = detect lysisDetection on lysisZone for 20s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Lysis QC gate
// Pass (BB2): lysisSignal > 0 -> Cell Tracker Orange
//             fluorescence drop confirmed in target cell,
//             neighbouring cells unaffected; proceed to
//             assay branches.
// Fail (BB3): lysisSignal <= 0 -> lysis failed (no drop,
//             or neighbouring cell affected); drain lysis
//             zone and retry on next target cell.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (lysisJoin).
// ============================================================

if (lysisSignal > 0) {
    dispose lysisZone
} else {
    drain lysisZone
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: lysisJoin
// Dispose lysis QC signal. Lysate flows through device and
// is subdivided by pneumatic valve routing into AB1 (Akt)
// and AB2 (GAPDH) chambers. Lysate mixed with assay buffer
// at 1:4 ratio by passive resistance-ratio mixing in 5 um
// channels. Valves (V1-V4) actuated with compressed air
// (30 psi) via solenoid valve manifold at 90 s after lysis
// (measured travel time from tip to reaction chambers) to
// trap assay mixture in chambers.
// Assay chambers monitored at 30 C on automated motorised
// stage (Prior Scientific H110) in heating chamber (Tokai
// Hit) placed on Olympus IX71 microscope.
// ============================================================

dispose lysisSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Akt kinase activity assay (chamber AB1).
//          Sox peptide sensor (10 uM substrate peptide) in
//          Akt assay buffer mixed 1:4 with lysate from AB1.
//          Assay mixture trapped in AB1 reaction chamber by
//          valve actuation (V1/V2 closed) at 90 s after lysis.
//          Fluorescence monitored every 30 s for >= 20 min
//          at 30 C using DAPI filter (ex 377 nm, em 447 nm,
//          Semrock), shutter (Uniblitz, 200 ms exposure).
//          Sox sensor phosphorylation by Akt generates
//          chelation-enhanced fluorescence (CSox fluorophore).
//          Activity = initial slope of fluorescence vs time.
//          LOD: 0.32 pg recombinant active Akt (vs 0.51 ng
//          on plate reader). ~1 ng total protein equivalent
//          per single HepG2 cell lysate.
//          Control: lysis buffer (no lysate) run in parallel.
//          aktKinaseDetection module abstracts the Sox sensor
//          fluorescence slope fitting (initial linear region).
//          NOTE: `mix` abstracts passive resistance-ratio
//          mixing of lysate with Akt assay buffer in 5 um
//          channels before valve closure traps mixture.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aktAssayMix = mix lysisBuffer with aktBuffer for 90s

heat aktAssayMix at 30c for 20m

aktSignal   = detect aktKinaseDetection on aktAssayMix for 20m

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Akt activity QC gate
// Pass (BB5): aktSignal > 0 -> Akt activity detected above
//             lysis buffer baseline; 'high Akt' phenotype
//             (insulin-responsive); dispose Akt assay mixture.
// Fail (BB6): aktSignal <= 0 -> Akt activity at or below
//             baseline; 'low Akt' phenotype (non-responsive
//             to insulin; p-value 0.35, consistent with
//             senescent morphology subgroup in Fig. 5a);
//             drain Akt assay mixture.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (aktJoin).
// ============================================================

if (aktSignal > 0) {
    dispose aktAssayMix
} else {
    drain aktAssayMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: aktJoin
// Dispose Akt QC signal. GAPDH assay branch begins.
// GAPDH serves as housekeeping loading control to normalise
// Akt activity per cell (Supplementary Fig. 9). GAPDH
// activity unaffected by insulin stimulation (p=0.98 for
// 'high Akt' cells; Fig. 5a dark red markers).
// ============================================================

dispose aktSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: GAPDH activity assay (chamber AB2).
//          GAPDH assay buffer (4 mM NAD+, 10 mM
//          glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate in 90 mM sodium
//          pyrophosphate pH 7.1 + 20 mM NaH2PO4 + 3 mM DTT)
//          mixed 1:4 with lysate from AB2 subdivision.
//          Assay mixture trapped in AB2 reaction chamber by
//          valve actuation (V3/V4 closed) at 90 s after lysis.
//          GAPDH converts NAD+ to NADH (fluorescent);
//          monitored on DAPI filter (ex 377 nm, em 447 nm)
//          every 30 s for >= 20 min at 30 C.
//          LOD lower than Akt (Fig. 4f) due to higher GAPDH
//          expression levels relative to Akt.
//          gapdhActivityDetection module abstracts NADH
//          fluorescence slope fitting (initial linear region).
//          NOTE: Simultaneously acquired with Akt assay (AB1
//          and AB2 chambers imaged on automated stage). Here
//          encoded sequentially for BioScript compatibility
//          (no concurrent parallel detect statements).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gapdhAssayMix = mix lysisBuffer with gapdhBuffer for 90s

heat gapdhAssayMix at 30c for 20m

gapdhSignal   = detect gapdhActivityDetection on gapdhAssayMix for 20m

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: GAPDH activity QC gate
// Pass (BB8): gapdhSignal > 0 -> GAPDH activity detected;
//             loading control confirmed; dispose GAPDH
//             assay mixture.
// Fail (BB9): gapdhSignal <= 0 -> GAPDH not detected
//             (possible lysate loss or chamber failure);
//             drain GAPDH assay mixture.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (gapdhSignal > 0) {
    dispose gapdhAssayMix
} else {
    drain gapdhAssayMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose GAPDH QC signal. Single-cell multiplexed assay
// cycle complete. Probe repositioned to next target cell
// for subsequent measurement (up to 4 cells in parallel
// using 4 chambers AB1-AB4; lysis is sequential per cell).
// ============================================================

dispose gapdhSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
